egin{pmatrix}1&2\\\\3&4\\end{pmatrix}+\\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\\\1&0\\end{pmatrix}$.","options":["$\\begin{pmatrix}1&3\\\\4&4\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}1&2\\\\3&4\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}0&2\\\\3&0\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}1&1\\\\1&1\\end{pmatrix}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"7dae1785598740646482de6b","time_limit":20},{"id":"la_batch4_matrix_addition_010","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"For same-size matrices, what is the $(i,j)$ entry of $A+B$?","options":["$a_{ij}+b_{ij}$","$a_{ii}+b_{jj}$","$a_{ij}b_{ij}$","$a_{ji}+b_{ji}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"e2ea7e28c1f2e1e6572469d8","time_limit":20},{"id":"la_batch4_matrix_addition_015","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Which matrix $X$ satisfies $X+\\begin{pmatrix}1&2\\\\3&4\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}0&0\\\\0&0\\end{pmatrix}$?","options":["$\\begin{pmatrix}-1&-2\\\\-3&-4\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}1&2\\\\3&4\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}4&3\\\\2&1\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}0&0\\\\0&0\\end{pmatrix}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a899b089e2424b21d038d19d","time_limit":30},{"id":"la_batch4_matrix_addition_005_curated20261027_001","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $\\boldsymbol{A}$, $\\boldsymbol{B}$, $\\boldsymbol{C}$ be $m\\times n$ matrices. Which statement is always true?","options":["$\\boldsymbol{A}+\\boldsymbol{B}=\\boldsymbol{B}+\\boldsymbol{A}$, because $a_{ij}+b_{ij}=b_{ij}+a_{ij}$ in the field.","$\\boldsymbol{A}\\boldsymbol{B}=\\boldsymbol{B}\\boldsymbol{A}$, because products are formed entry by entry like sums.","$\\boldsymbol{A}-\\boldsymbol{B}=\\boldsymbol{B}-\\boldsymbol{A}$, because subtraction is addition of $-\\boldsymbol{B}$.","$(\\boldsymbol{A}+\\boldsymbol{B})+\\boldsymbol{C}=\\boldsymbol{A}+(\\boldsymbol{B}+\\boldsymbol{C})$ holds only when $m=n$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"4626eb71ecf97674cd35ef62","time_limit":35},{"id":"year_1_1b_math_ii_linear_algebra_matrix_addition_f5ff8282_topup20261028_001","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $\\boldsymbol{A}$ and $\\boldsymbol{B}$ be real $2\\times3$ matrices and $\\boldsymbol{x}\\in\\mathbb{R}^3$ a column vector with $\\boldsymbol{A}\\boldsymbol{x}=\\begin{pmatrix}2\\\\-1\\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\boldsymbol{B}\\boldsymbol{x}=\\begin{pmatrix}3\\\\5\\end{pmatrix}$. What can be said about $(\\boldsymbol{A}+\\boldsymbol{B})\\boldsymbol{x}$?","options":["It cannot be found without the entries of $\\boldsymbol{A}$ and $\\boldsymbol{B}$.","It equals $\\begin{pmatrix}6\\\\-5\\end{pmatrix}$.","It equals $\\begin{pmatrix}5\\\\4\\end{pmatrix}$.","It is undefined, since only square matrices can be added."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"5991ca58a7dd371345d380f7","time_limit":35}]}}